## Dependencies

Everything Polyxd depends on at runtime or to build is fetched from npm rather
than vendored, so the licences below are recorded rather than reproduced.

Apache-2.0: playwright
MIT: react, react-dom, radix-ui, ajv, ajv-formats, vite, @vitejs/plugin-react,
     marked, lenis, @types/react, @types/react-dom
MIT OR Apache-2.0: wrangler, @cloudflare/workers-types

Two need a word.

**axe-core** (Mozilla Public License 2.0) runs inside the verifier's rendered
audit. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: it attaches to modified MPL files, and
axe-core is used unmodified, as a library. No Polyxd file is covered by it.

**GSAP** (https://gsap.com/standard-license) drives the motion on polyxd.com
only, and is not an OSI-approved licence. It is not used by the spec, the
renderer, the packs or the verifier, none of which it can reach; and no GSAP
file is committed to this repository — the site's build copies them out of
node_modules into its own output. Anyone building the site is therefore subject
to GSAP's licence, and anyone using the rest of Polyxd is not.


## Fonts

No font files are distributed. polyxd.com loads its typefaces from Google Fonts
at request time, and a design-system pack names the typeface its system
specifies without shipping it — a pack that asks for Adobe Clean, for example,
names an open metric-compatible fallback for anyone who does not have it.
